From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aravind Krishnan <aravind.krishnan@alifsemi.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: rkisp1: Cap the ARX3A0 exposure at the CPI init value

In a dim scene the AGC measured the frame about 100x below its target
and asked for the maximum exposure, 0xA47A lines (frame length minus
one). From the first AGC result onward the frames came back flat at the
sensor pedestal (mean Y about 38) instead of the dim scene (mean Y
about 56).

Cap the AGC exposure at the init-table coarse integration, 0x366A, so
a dim scene is brightened with analogue gain. Apply the same limit
where the exposure control is written.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Alif ARX3A0 / ISP8000Pico board tuning]
Signed-off-by: Aravind Krishnan <aravind.krishnan@alifsemi.com>
---

--- a/src/ipa/rkisp1/rkisp1.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/rkisp1/rkisp1.cpp
@@ -304,11 +304,14 @@
 	context_.configuration.sensor.minExposureTime =
 		minExposure * context_.configuration.sensor.lineDuration;
 	/*
-	 * The RAW10 init table programs frame length 0xA47B. Coarse
-	 * integration above that does not produce a frame. 65535 is
-	 * the old V4L2 max and is what made the start/end frames black.
+	 * The RAW10 init table programs frame length 0xA47B, and coarse
+	 * integration above that does not produce a frame. In a dim scene
+	 * the AGC also drove R0x3012 to 0xA47A (frame length minus one)
+	 * and the frames came back flat at the sensor pedestal. Cap the
+	 * AGC at the init-table integration and let it use analogue gain
+	 * for the rest.
 	 */
-	constexpr int32_t kMaxCoarseLines = 0xA47A;
+	constexpr int32_t kMaxCoarseLines = 0x366A;
 	if (maxExposure > kMaxCoarseLines)
 		maxExposure = kMaxCoarseLines;
 	context_.configuration.sensor.maxExposureTime =
@@ -509,7 +512,7 @@
 
 	if (exposure < static_cast<uint32_t>(std::max(minExposure, 1)))
 		exposure = defExposure > 0 ? defExposure : 1;
-	constexpr uint32_t kMaxCoarseLines = 0xA47A;
+	constexpr uint32_t kMaxCoarseLines = 0x366A;
 	uint32_t maxLines = kMaxCoarseLines;
 	if (maxExposure > 0 && static_cast<uint32_t>(maxExposure) < maxLines)
 		maxLines = maxExposure;
